$ =========================================================================
$ val_wing_taper_dihedral.bdf
$ Example wing — 5 deg dihedral, taper 0.80
$
$ The NO-TWIST half of an A/B pair with val_wing_taper_dihedral_twist.bdf, which is
$ this deck plus a 0 -> -2 deg linear washout W2GJ and nothing else.  The pair is the
$ worked example in docs/10_standard/05a_aero_vlm.md for what a W2GJ twist does to the
$ load: rigid VLM at alpha = 3 deg gives CL = 0.2669 here against 0.1851 with washout.
$ Do not delete this deck as a duplicate — without it the comparison has no baseline,
$ and it is the 'taper_dih' canted-deck case in tests/aero/test_vae3_cross_check.py.
$
$ PLANFORM (full span, modelled as two CAERO1 surfaces):
$   Root chord cr = 1.000, tip chord ct = 0.800 (taper 0.80)
$   Root LE at (0, 0, 0); LE unswept (X4 = 0)
$   Dihedral Gamma = 5.0 deg about the root chord (x-axis)
$     cosG = 0.99619470, sinG = 0.08715574
$   Surface semi-span S = 5.000
$     stbd tip LE = (0, 4.98097349, 0.43577871)
$     port tip LE = (0, -4.98097349, 0.43577871)
$
$ REFERENCE GEOMETRY (full-span; AEROS):
$   CREF = 0.9000 (mean chord), BREF = 10.000 (surface span 2S),
$   SREF = 9.000 (full planform area).  SYMXZ = SYMXY = 0 (full-span).
$
$ MESH: 10 spanwise x 4 chordwise per half = 40 boxes/half,
$   80 boxes total.  Box ordering is row-major (span slow, chord fast).
$
$ Coordinate system: X = freestream, Y = starboard, Z = up.
$ Pure rigid VLM example — NO structural model, NO splines.
$ Loads in the viewer Aero tab (set AoA, press Compute Aero).
$ =========================================================================
$
SOL 101
$
SUBCASE 1
  TITLE = Tapered 5deg-dihedral wing — rigid VLM (no twist)
$
BEGIN BULK
$
$ ----------------------------------------------------------- AERO REFERENCE
$ ACSID RCSID  CREF  BREF  SREF  SYMXZ SYMXY
AEROS,  0,  0,  0.9000,  10.000,  9.000,  0,  0
$
PAERO1, 1
$
$ ---- Starboard half: root (0,0,0) c=1.000 -> tip (0.0, 4.980973, 0.435779) c=0.800
$ CAERO1  EID  PID CP NSPAN NCHORD LSPAN LCHORD IGID
CAERO1, 100, 1, 0, 10, 4, 0, 0, 1
+, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0000, 0.0, 4.98097349, 0.43577871, 0.8000
$
$ ---- Port half: root (0,0,0) c=1.000 -> tip (0.0, -4.980973, 0.435779) c=0.800
CAERO1, 150, 1, 0, 10, 4, 0, 0, 1
+, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0000, 0.0, -4.98097349, 0.43577871, 0.8000
$
ENDDATA
